# Route Resolution Spec

## Scope

Frontend/backend resolution for `/`, custom pages, documentation/forum-doc deep
links, public KJV deep links, landing-page swaps, and CDN-safe page fetching.

## Load when

Changing `PageBuilder`, `usePageData`, page routes, Bible URL parsing, landing
page config, CDN/cache behavior, or page WebSocket events.

## Owns

- Backend: `backend/internal/page/handler.go`, `backend/internal/page/service.go`
- Frontend: `frontend/src/pages/index/index.tsx`,
  `frontend/src/components/page/PageBuilder.tsx`,
  `frontend/src/hooks/usePageData.ts`, `frontend/src/pages/kjv/index.tsx`,
  `frontend/src/components/bible/location.ts`
- Bible backend: `backend/internal/bible/handler.go`
- Config key: `site_config.landing_page_slug`
- Documentation routes: `frontend/src/pages/documentation/*`,
  `backend/internal/documentation/*`, `backend/internal/forum/handler.go`

## Cold Load `/`

1. Browser requests `/`; backend serves SSR-injected SPA HTML.
2. React mounts index page and `PageBuilder` with no explicit slug.
3. Frontend calls `GET /pages/landing-slug`.
4. Frontend fetches `GET /pages/{slug}` for the resolved slug.

`/pages/index` remains as a legacy inline landing endpoint but is not the primary
frontend path because it is a single CDN cache key for different possible pages.

## Landing Swap

Current backend route:

| Method | Path | Body | Result |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `POST` | `/pages/{id}/set-homepage` | none | Stores that page's slug in `landing_page_slug` |

Backend dispatch after success:

| Channel | Action | Payload |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `page:update` | `landing_page_changed` | `{ id, slug, partial: true }` |
| `config:update` | `landing_page_updated` | `{ slug }` |

Clients in index mode refetch through the slug resolution path after the
content-free landing invalidation. `landing_page_updated` is a fallback signal
for UI badges and missed page pushes.

## Documentation Deep Links

- `/doc` catalogs active public documentation sets; `/doc/{set}` opens its
  first ordered guide and `/doc/{set}/{guide}` is the canonical guide URL.
- `/forum/docs/{categoryId}/{threadId}` presents the authoritative forum thread;
  moved threads canonicalize to their current category ID.
- Documentation-set slugs are tenant-local human identifiers. Forum-doc links
  use numeric category/thread IDs because forum names are mutable.
- Recognized public/unlisted documentation routes receive database-backed SSR
  metadata. Unknown/deleted/private resources resolve as absence unless the
  authenticated API later authorizes the SPA user.

## Public KJV Deep Links

| Form | Contract |
| --- | --- |
| `/kjv` | Opens the public Bible browser; validated saved preferences may restore selection without changing the base URL |
| `/kjv?bt=Matthew&c=6&v=25&o=1` | Legacy query form; all four fields are required when any is present |
| `/kjv/matthew/6/25/open` | Path form; the final segment is exactly `open` or `closed` |

The first complete URL state is authoritative over local preferences. Book
titles/slugs are matched case-insensitively after space/underscore normalization,
with `Psalm` retained as an alias for canonical `Psalms`. UI navigation preserves
the URL form used to enter the reader. Canonicalization uses history replacement;
user navigation pushes history, while automatic narration replaces the current
coordinate.

## Page Mutations

- `PUT /pages/{id}` returns the authoritative updated page to the sender.
- Page writes broadcast a content-free partial invalidation on `page:{id}`.
- Other clients refetch if slug/id matches their current page.
- Deletion broadcasts `page:update page_deleted` with `{ id, slug }`.
- Page deletion clears `landing_page_slug` in the same transaction when the
  deleted page is current. Restoring a page never silently selects it as the
  homepage; the user must invoke `set-homepage` explicitly.
- Deleted pages are absent from slug, landing, and browse reads.

## Invariants

- No `is_index` column; homepage selection is only `landing_page_slug`.
- Do not introduce redirects for page API correctness.
- Use `landing-slug => slug fetch` for cold landing loads.
- Landing swap must cancel queued local page saves before changing pages.
- Incoming page broadcasts must preserve per-user local fields such as `is_liked`
  and `can_delete` when those are absent from the broadcast.
- Invalid or incomplete KJV deep links expose a visible error and never render
  persisted scripture as if the supplied coordinate had resolved.

## Anti-patterns

- Calling `/pages/index` as the default frontend landing fetch.
- Sending only a slug for landing changes; clients need full page data to avoid
  stale CDN reads.
- Letting delayed saves from the old page fire after a landing/page swap.

